  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Orilissa (elagolix), Oriahnn (elagolix/estradiol/norethindrone acetate), and Myfembree (relugolix/estradiol/norethindrone acetate) in the single orilissa pack. Version 3; approval 09/16/2022; effective 2022-11-01.",
    "Encoded: product-specific approval criteria and shared/product-specific denials. Indication choices include diagnosis and treatment purpose. FDA usage describes premenopausal women for fibroid-associated heavy menstrual bleeding. Prior trials are attestations; the source does not provide intolerance or contraindication exceptions.",
    "Cautions (notes only): potentially irreversible bone loss; reduced ability to recognize pregnancy; increased suicidal ideation and mood disorders; increased liver transaminases (monitor LFTs); potential decreased efficacy of estrogen-containing oral contraceptives.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 6 months. Orilissa reauthorization up to 12 months for the 150mg dose only. Oriahnn and Myfembree reauthorization each up to 12 months, not to exceed 24 months total treatment.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): Orilissa 30 × 150mg tablets/month or 60 × 200mg tablets/month; Oriahnn 56 capsules in 4 blister packs; Myfembree 30 capsules per 30 days (source wording). No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "PDL status unknown. Remaining gaps: documentation verification, cautions, dosing, duration, reauthorization and quantity limits require manual review."
  ],
